{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00305",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.82,
      "end_seconds": 8.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.9,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.92,
      "end_seconds": 15.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 15.53,
      "end_seconds": 17.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.53,
      "end_seconds": 21.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.77,
      "end_seconds": 24.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.62,
      "end_seconds": 27.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.04,
      "end_seconds": 39.07,
      "duration_seconds": 11.03,
      "text": "For two months, I'd say. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.81,
      "end_seconds": 46.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.71,
      "end_seconds": 59.35,
      "duration_seconds": 12.64,
      "text": "Yes, coffee and stress. That makes it worse. It's severe, honestly. And a fluttering in the chest, too. With fluttering in the chest, about a six out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.03,
      "end_seconds": 61.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Have you had lightheadedness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.46,
      "end_seconds": 65.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had that since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.72,
      "end_seconds": 69.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.02,
      "end_seconds": 79.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "Maybe a five out of ten on a bad day. And I've been sweating as well, for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.57,
      "end_seconds": 84.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.76,
      "end_seconds": 88.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "So, thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.52,
      "end_seconds": 93.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any fainting or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.76,
      "end_seconds": 96.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.97,
      "end_seconds": 101.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Okay, any weight loss or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.69,
      "end_seconds": 104.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.33,
      "end_seconds": 107.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.79,
      "end_seconds": 110.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.97,
      "end_seconds": 114.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.76,
      "end_seconds": 115.56,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.5,
      "end_seconds": 134.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.65,
      "end_seconds": 139.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Okay, so I have high blood pressure, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.69,
      "end_seconds": 141.39,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.05,
      "end_seconds": 145.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "I've had an underactive thyroid for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.99,
      "end_seconds": 169.13,
      "duration_seconds": 22.14,
      "text": "Okay, high blood pressure, that's already on your record. Good to know. Right, so that's your known an underactive thyroid. We'll keep that in mind today. It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.72,
      "end_seconds": 172.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.36,
      "end_seconds": 176.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.79,
      "end_seconds": 187.96,
      "duration_seconds": 10.17,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.89,
      "end_seconds": 191.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "One moment, I'm updating your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.64,
      "end_seconds": 206.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Good, where were we. What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.23,
      "end_seconds": 212.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "I'm on losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 214.34,
      "end_seconds": 218.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 100 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.25,
      "end_seconds": 222.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.56,
      "end_seconds": 227.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Hmm, not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.81,
      "end_seconds": 242.38,
      "duration_seconds": 13.57,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.77,
      "end_seconds": 246.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Thank you, um, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 247.29,
      "end_seconds": 254.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Respiratory rate 19, BP is 124 over 73, pulse is 121 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.53,
      "end_seconds": 271.25,
      "duration_seconds": 15.72,
      "text": "Good, thank you. What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.7,
      "end_seconds": 274.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Yeah, I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.24,
      "end_seconds": 278.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.15,
      "end_seconds": 280.85,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.7,
      "end_seconds": 284.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.93,
      "end_seconds": 294.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Pulse is irregular right now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.03,
      "end_seconds": 296.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.99,
      "end_seconds": 299.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "I'll just listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.15,
      "end_seconds": 320.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "No murmurs and the neck veins aren't distended."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.19,
      "end_seconds": 334.8,
      "duration_seconds": 11.61,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.63,
      "end_seconds": 347.39,
      "duration_seconds": 11.76,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.93,
      "end_seconds": 367.41,
      "duration_seconds": 18.48,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. This looks most like palpitations with an unclear cause. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I'd also keep too much caffeine in mind. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had palpitations for two months, severe, and no fainting or leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.89,
      "end_seconds": 369.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.6,
      "end_seconds": 374.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.9,
      "end_seconds": 375.6,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.91,
      "end_seconds": 396.49,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Let's get an echocardiogram, for palpitations. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 399.57,
      "end_seconds": 402.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "We've already done an ECG this morning, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.85,
      "end_seconds": 432.8,
      "duration_seconds": 28.95,
      "text": "Good, thank you. I'd like to arrange a thyroid test for palpitations. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'd like you to take metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day, until we review. You take it by mouth. It's for palpitations. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Cut back on tea, coffee and energy drinks, and note the time whenever it happens."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.45,
      "end_seconds": 448.75,
      "duration_seconds": 15.3,
      "text": "Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 449.86,
      "end_seconds": 451.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 452.54,
      "end_seconds": 460.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you faint or have chest pain with the racing, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 461.22,
      "end_seconds": 462.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 464.2,
      "end_seconds": 472.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in two weeks. Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 473.77,
      "end_seconds": 481.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "So, I take the metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 482.54,
      "end_seconds": 487.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 488.66,
      "end_seconds": 492.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 492.86,
      "end_seconds": 493.56,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}